# Local overrides for the one-card engine: copy to engines/one-card/env/tp1-local.env (git-ignored) and uncomment
# what you change. Values here win over engines/one-card/env/tp1-hotcold.env. Apply with `docker compose up -d`.
# Format: KEY=value, no quotes, no variable expansion (docker env-file rules).

# --- hot experts (of 512 per layer): each one is 116 MiB of VRAM instead of host RAM ----------------------------------
# Raise while the boot still reaches "KV cache size" with enough KV for --max-model-len; lower if loading runs out of VRAM.
#B70_MOE_HOT_EXPERTS=96

# --- cold-expert prefetch for prefill: ~2 GiB VRAM at TP 1 -------------------------------------------------------------
# Off: ~17 more hot experts fit (faster decode), prefill slower.
#B70_MOE_COLD_PREFETCH=0

# --- extra `vllm serve` flags (appended to engines/one-card/args/serve-tp1.args; the last value of a flag wins) --------
#EXTRA_ARGS=--max-model-len 32768
#EXTRA_ARGS=--max-model-len 131072

# --- another flag file (e.g. without MTP: copy serve-tp1.args to serve-tp1.local.args and delete --speculative-config)
#SERVE_ARGS_FILE=/b70-engines/one-card/args/serve-tp1.local.args
